[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3038401766","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108286#issuecomment-3038401766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108286","id":3038401766,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61GlTm","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-05T07:49:26Z","updated_at":"2025-07-05T07:51:14Z","body":"Confirmed on `v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]`.\n\nNote that replacing the texture with a new ViewportTexture is not required to resolve the issue, simply resetting the selected Viewport is sufficient to have it render correctly (it has to be clicking the reset button then re-selecting, leaving the viewport selected and then selecting it again does not work). Also for clarity, the ViewportTexture is not being replaced with the PlaceholderTexture in the scene/`.tscn` file, it is just rendering with the PlaceholderTexture pattern.\n\nIf I add a Camera3D to the root node in the MRP, then start the scene (with or without applying the fix), it always seems to render the PlaceholderTexture pattern (see screenshot where you can see it rendering correctly in editor but not in the game window). I am also observing this behaviour without the shader, and just creating a new material with Albedo > Texture set to ViewportTexture. I also tried with a 2D scene in the SubViewport and it still occurs the same way.\n\n<img width=\"1680\" height=\"1050\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bb68e621-bf0c-4f4e-80b6-10140d8a81d5\" />\n\nI cannot see anything obviously wrong about the scene by inspecting directly or reading the `.tscn` file.\n\n```\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.5.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 (Apple7) - Apple M1 (8 threads)\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3038401766/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3039605648","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108286#issuecomment-3039605648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108286","id":3039605648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61LLOQ","user":{"login":"zedzee37","id":65473813,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NDczODEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65473813?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37","html_url":"https://github.com/zedzee37","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-05T18:39:23Z","updated_at":"2025-07-05T18:39:23Z","body":"after looking into it, it appears that the SubViewport is null when the resource is loaded. I assume this is because it tries to load the ViewportTexture resource before the SubViewport.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3039605648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3039771025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108286#issuecomment-3039771025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108286","id":3039771025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61LzmR","user":{"login":"zedzee37","id":65473813,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NDczODEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65473813?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37","html_url":"https://github.com/zedzee37","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zedzee37/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-05T19:17:54Z","updated_at":"2025-07-05T19:17:54Z","body":"I have found a solution, I am going to submit a PR shortly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3039771025/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3040464167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108286#issuecomment-3040464167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108286","id":3040464167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61Oc0n","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-06T00:03:02Z","updated_at":"2025-07-06T00:49:51Z","body":"This is not a bug, you just need to enable all `resource_local_to_scene` on the resource chain from the node to the `ViewportTexture`. The `resource_local_to_scene` of `ShaderMaterial` is missed in the MRP.\n\nThe setup of `ViewportTexture` configured in `tscn` is extremely dependent on `Viewport` (in the same scene, so `resource_local_to_scene` is enabled by default). In other words, it is extremely dependent on `local_scene` (the node referenced by `get_local_scene()`).\n\nFor resource chains, passing `local_scene` requires that the parent resource that uses this resource also has `resource_local_to_scene` enabled.\n\n\nChain in MRP:\n```\n(Quad:mesh) --> QuadMesh:material --> ShaderMaterial:shader_parameter/ScreenTexture --> ViewportTexture\n\n^\"Quad:mesh:material:shader_parameter/ScreenTexture\"\n```\n\nIn MRP, the passing of `local_scene` is broken.\n\nPerhaps this should be emphasized in the documentation.\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3040464167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3040515656","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108286#issuecomment-3040515656","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108286","id":3040515656,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61OpZI","user":{"login":"lupuchard","id":2514990,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MTQ5OTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2514990?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard","html_url":"https://github.com/lupuchard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lupuchard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-06T01:31:14Z","updated_at":"2025-07-06T01:31:14Z","body":"> The `resource_local_to_scene` of `ShaderMaterial` is missed in the MRP.\n\nIt is enabled on the material in the MRP, but not on the `QuadMesh`.\n\nWhen you try to add a ViewportTexture to the material without `resource_local_to_scene` checked you get a popup telling you about the local to scene requirement:\n<img width=\"665\" height=\"162\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/66c5f30a-9e77-4b3c-9ce4-5e8e58177902\" />\n\nI must have missed the \"and all resources containing it up to a node\" part of the warning. I guess the bug here is that this popup only seems to trigger when the direct parent isn't local to scene, when it should be checking the the entire chain.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3040515656/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3040532105","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108286#issuecomment-3040532105","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108286","id":3040532105,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61OtaJ","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-06T02:00:33Z","updated_at":"2025-07-06T02:00:33Z","body":"> ... when it should be checking the the entire chain.\n\nActually it just checks that you added a `ViewportTexture`. Because it doesn't always check the property. And the resource is usually not aware of who uses it. \n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3040532105/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]